hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1095","Chapter on the prohibition of mutilation, 1133 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Hayyaj: that a boy - perhaps he said: I am Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Hayyaj: that a boy - perhaps he said to his father - ran away, so he vowed that if he got hold of him he would cut off a part of him. When he came back to him, he sent me to Imran ibn Husayn, so I asked him. Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever wishes to free his slave or to expiate his oath, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge us to give charity and forbade mutilation. 1134 - He said: So I went to Samurah, and he said the like of what Imran had said."
